  "problem": "$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x, & x\\in [-\\frac{\\pi }{2},0] \\\\ {e}^{x}, & x\\in (0,\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the function $F(x)$ shown above. Find the value to which the Fourier series of the $\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is converging when $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$\n\nThe Fourier series converges to {{field-1}} when $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$",
